# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
"""Generate Beryllium's Chromium branding resources from the art set.

Inputs:  artwork/logo/ (cut from the art set v2 sheet by extract-art-sheet)
Outputs: artwork/icons/ (app icons at the desktop sizes)
         branding/chromium/ (Chromium-specific files)
         branding/chromium/beryllium_resources.txt (destination list in the
         format of Helium's utils/replace_resources.py)
         All committed; the build does not run this tool.

What is generated:
  - product and desktop icons: the colour emblem (orb, "Be", two orbits)
    from 48 px up; the plain colour orb at 16 to 32 px, where the orbits
    would blur into the orb (the art set has a size ramp of each)
  - lockups (emblem + "Beryllium"): product_logo{,_white}{,_200}.png at
    Helium's sizes, and product_logo_name_22{,_white}.png at Chromium's
  - product_logo.svg and the onboarding logo: the colour emblem, embedded
    as PNG (Chromium's WebUI pages allow data: images)
  - the vector glyph, where Chromium needs vectors (.icon files: one
    colour, one monochrome in the theme colour) and the 22 px monochrome
    PNG: the plain orb with "Be", drawn to the art's proportions

Needs Pillow and fontTools, and Inter Bold (close to the art's lettering):
  make-chromium-branding [--font /path/to/Inter-Bold.otf] [--check]
--check regenerates into a temporary directory and fails if anything
differs from the committed files.
"""

